# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
# Libraries should not include pubspec.lock
**/pubspec.lock
**/doc/api/
**/.dart_tool/
**/.flutter-plugins
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
**/build/
**/coverage/

# Android related
# The Gradle wrapper (gradlew, gradlew.bat, gradle-wrapper.jar) is deliberately
# checked in, against the Flutter template's default: it pins the Gradle version
# this plugin is built and tested against, and CI needs it to run the Android
# module's unit tests. Do not re-add ignore rules for it -- `dart pub publish`
# rejects a package whose checked-in files are gitignored.
**/.gradle
**/android/**/captures/
**/android/**/local.properties
**/android/**/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
**/android/**/*.keystore
**/android/**/*.jks
**/android/**/key.properties
**/.cxx/

# iOS related (for future)
**/ios/.symlinks/
**/ios/Pods/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
**/ios/Flutter/App.framework
**/ios/Flutter/Flutter.framework
**/ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
**/ios/ServiceDefinitions.json

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Test related
**/coverage/
**/.test_coverage.dart

# Generated files
*.g.dart
*.freezed.dart
*.mocks.dart

# Working notes -- the plan and progress files at the repository root.
# Anchored: an unanchored `docs/` matches a directory of that name at ANY depth,
# which silently swallowed the findings notes shipped beside the iOS widget
# templates. Nothing failed; the file simply never entered git.
/docs/

